1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 Bc5 5. Be3 Bb6 6. Nc3 d6 7. h3 O-O 8. Qd2
Nd4 9. Bxd4 exd4 10. Ne2 c5 11. Nf4 Bd7 12. O-O Bc6 13. Nd5 Nxd5 14. exd5 Bd7
15. a3 Qf6 16. Ng5 Qg6 17. Kh2 h6 18. Nf3 f5 19. b4 f4 20. Rae1 Qh5 21. Qd1 Bg4
22. Re7 Rae8 23. Rfe1 Rxe7 24. Rxe7 Bc8 25. Qe2 cxb4 26. axb4 Bd8 27. Re6 Bxe6
28. Qxe6+ Qf7 29. Qxd6 Qf6 30. Qd7 Kh7 31. Qxb7 Qb6 32. Qd7 Bc7 33. b5 Qb8 34.
Qg4 Qe8 35. Nxd4 Bb6 36. Ne6 Rf7 37. d4 Qe7 38. Bd3+ Kg8 39. Qg6 Rf6 40. Qh7+
Kf7 41. Qxg7+ Ke8 42. Qg8+ Kd7 43. Qg4 Qd6 44. c4 {Source: L'Italia
Scacchistica, Vol.17, no.19, 1 October 1927, p5. The score of this game is
identical to the one found on databases of Havasi-Romi, London Olympiad, round
5, 21.07.1927. I am grateful to Ulrich Tamm for searching out a primary source
for this game (confirmation received 21 December 2023). Now that it has been
found, I'm reversing my original assumption that the Havasi-Romi score was the
correct one. It is to be noted that the Havasi-Romi score does not appear in
the London 1927 booklet by Ken Whyld published by The Chess Player in 2001,
and so far no primary source has been found, so the mix-up must have occurred
in the past 20 years.} 1-0

